# Routes Inventory

## API Base
- API host: `https://api.mytitan.co.uk`
- Main route sources: `api/src/**/*.controller.ts`

## Public / Unauthenticated Routes
- `GET /health`
- `POST /auth/signup`
- `POST /auth/login`
- `POST /auth/forgot-password` (always 202 pattern)
- `POST /auth/reset-password`
- `POST /auth/verify-email`
- `POST /users/accept-invite`
- Public job portal:
  - `GET /public/job/:token`
  - `GET /public/job/:token/pdf`
  - `POST /public/job/:token/approve`
  - `POST /public/job/:token/decline`
  - `POST /public/job/:token/sign`
  - `POST /public/job/:token/checkout`
  - `GET /public/job/:token/payment-status`
- Public booking portal:
  - `GET /public/booking/:token/config`
  - `GET /public/booking/:token/slots`
  - `POST /public/booking/:token`
  - `GET /public/ics/:token`
- :
  - `POST /public/-login` (404 when flag off)
- Webhooks:
  - `POST /stripe/webhook`
  - `POST /billing/webhook`

## Auth-Guarded Areas (Jwt + roles in most controllers)
Common guard pattern:
- `@UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard, RolesGuard)`

Examples:
- Jobs: `/jobs`, `/jobs/board`, `/jobs/board-v2`, `/jobs/bulk`, `/jobs/bulk-v2`
- Command centre views: `/board-views`, `/command-centre/*`
- CRM/trade accounts: `/trade-accounts/*`, `/crm/accounts/*`
- Booking pro/internal: `/booking/*`, `/bookings/*`
- Inventory: `/inventory/*`
- Locations: `/locations/*`, `/me/location`
- Tenant/admin settings: `/tenant/settings`, `/users/*`, `/integrations/*`, `/billing/*`
- Notifications: `/notifications`, `/notifications/preferences`

## Guard Behavior Validation (live smoke)
Ran:
- `/opt/mytitan/scripts/ops-core-smoke.sh`
- `/opt/mytitan/scripts/-polish-smoke.sh`

Observed:
- `GET /jobs/board-v2 -> 401`
- `GET /booking/services -> 401`
- `GET /crm/accounts/search -> 401`
- `GET /notifications -> 401`
- `GET /notifications/preferences -> 401`
- `PATCH /notifications/preferences -> 401`
- `POST /jobs/bulk-v2 -> 401`

Conclusion: key guarded surfaces are returning auth challenge (`401`) rather than `404`.

## Stripe Webhook Handling
Files:
- `api/src/main.ts` (raw body enabled for webhook routes)
- `api/src/billing/billing.controller.ts`
- `api/src/billing/billing.service.ts`

Mechanics:
- Raw body preserved via Express `raw()` middleware for `/stripe/webhook` and `/billing/webhook`.
- Signature verification via `stripe.webhooks.constructEvent(payload, signature, secret)`.
- Event handling for:
  - `checkout.session.completed`
  - `customer.subscription.created|updated|deleted`
  - `invoice.paid|invoice.payment_failed`

Idempotency approach:
- No explicit processed-event table keyed by Stripe `event.id`.
- Uses `upsert`/state writes that are mostly naturally idempotent, but duplicate event replay is not explicitly tracked.

